  "solution": {
    "text": "The actual nitrosation agent is the nitrosyl cation,  <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math>  which is formed as follows<br/><br/> <img src=\"assets\\st0028_46050723325e.jpeg\"/> <br/><br/>Aromatic tertiary amine i.e., N, N-dimethylaniline, undergo electrophilic substitution with nitrosonium ion at p-position of phenyl ring."
